basename - extract the last component of a pathname

SYNOPSIS
    basename path [suffix]

DESCRIPTION
    Strip trailing slashes and print the final component of path. The root
    pathname produces a single slash. If suffix matches the end of the
    result and is shorter than it, remove that suffix.

EXAMPLES
    basename /tmp/report.txt .txt prints report.

SEE ALSO
    dirname(1), pwd(1)
